2.6799999997,1209358.5480000004]]},"gpx_pois":"{\"type\":\"FeatureCollection\",\"features\":[{\"type\":\"Feature\",\"geometry\":{\"type\":\"Point\",\"coordinates\":[2695154.194098134,1209360.9137676028]},\"properties\":{\"name\":\"A\"}},{\"type\":\"Feature\",\"geometry\":{\"type\":\"Point\",\"coordinates\":[2695041.778888731,1209504.5554239827]},\"properties\":{\"name\":\"B\"}}]}","id":713727,"photos":[],"route_id":4136,"show_end":true,"show_start":true,"style":"plain","title":"Holzegg – bend 22","type":"course","route_type":"mountain_hiking","discipline":"mountain_hiking"},{"alternative":false,"description":"From the bend ascend ca. 25 metres in a slabby gully or on its right rim, until a blue arrow points left. From here on, the itinerary is marked. On a faint path almost horizontally traverse the grassy face («Gross Plangg» on the map) to reach a small tree grove and the first fixed ropes. Descend a few metres to go south-westward on a ledge blasted out of the rock and equipped with a number of safety features. On a narrow, slightly descending path at the foot of vertical limestone walls traverse the south-west face to reach Nollenbrünneli (small water well).\nAlong the rock walls continue to descend to a distinct gully, which you reach on an exposed ledge with fixed ropes. Traverse the gully and ascend a slab to Mythenmatt, a characteristic steep meadow, which on the map is distinctively charted as a triangle 200 metres west of the summit. The faint path disappearing and the scarce markings pointing to the left part of the meadow, you choose your own way to traverse. \nOn the upper, northern rim of Mythenmatt you come across a sparsely forested grassy ridge, which step by step transforms into the rocky north-west ridge. The so-called Rot Grätli has two steep steps to overcome. They are not really difficult, but fairly exposed. Finally, crossing a rock crevasse you reach the summit.","download_end":false,"download_start":false,"geom":{"type":"LineString","coordin